.TH HTTP_RESPONSE_FREE 3
.SH NAME
http_response_free \- free a response
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <http.h>
.P
.BI "void http_response_free(http_response* " r ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR http_response_free ()
frees the data and the multipart boundary of the response and the response itself. It does not take it out of the list
.IR h->response ;
.BR http_free (3)
frees them all.
.SH SEE ALSO
http_response_new(3), http_free(3)
